e that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2x+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n    Therefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279923 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2776554-94ce-5c25-b838-16fdfceddb1c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation With Rearranging"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2423c71-954f-5cce-8aac-46437ddebfac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279925} {:answer/id #uuid "64a3b3cc-f3a8-5a70-a7b1-0f10e1c4ea13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279926} {:answer/id #uuid "cddc2688-3410-5d85-b2da-620a3e01508b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279927} {:answer/id #uuid "f96123ac-7c3c-5fac-b059-747529406b19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279928} {:answer/id #uuid "7438bbdd-fefd-5186-a042-8bfb27951987" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279929}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2423c71-954f-5cce-8aac-46437ddebfac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279925} :answer-field/id #uuid "5772e640-debb-51f0-9250-b51e9acae784" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279924}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "774edb89-af5c-5c1e-9a68-335238aae11f" :question/math-academy-id "q-12011" :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation  $T$, where\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}y-3x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, rewrite the order of the variables in the usual way:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}-3x+y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe require a $2\\times 2$ matrix $T$ such that\n    \n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3x+y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3x+y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n    Therefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation  $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279930 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd0537f8-b091-580a-974e-8e928d54939d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Under a Linear Transformation Given its Standard Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0c4b647-4efd-57c3-9cd2-c4083a5c7db0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279932} {:answer/id #uuid "e519e0d8-4050-517c-b8d9-73d358fac112" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279933} {:answer/id #uuid "c4e62442-ffaf-5417-a0fb-dfa0d8e4a35a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279934} {:answer/id #uuid "a1913060-83ac-5900-8fb5-c66fe1b0cb60" :answer/type {: