776554-94ce-5c25-b838-16fdfceddb1c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation With Rearranging"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad5590b6-b5ba-564b-a260-08e0f9738eb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -12 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280045} {:answer/id #uuid "5f6a30b6-75c2-5b6d-bb9b-f588b58fb95b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 12 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280046} {:answer/id #uuid "81af885c-1d29-531c-bdf3-0f92b6f09443" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-12 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280047} {:answer/id #uuid "17f987f0-83a9-5064-b1f4-2e58832dfc43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 12 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280048} {:answer/id #uuid "731f0292-8b03-527c-8cea-dffb6ef7de88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 11 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280049}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81af885c-1d29-531c-bdf3-0f92b6f09443" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-12 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280047} :answer-field/id #uuid "26f370d7-c42d-528c-a730-8e2a0bd45d0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280044}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "275b123a-ba31-5124-8553-0cbb81013af7" :question/math-academy-id "q-8301" :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation $T$, where\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}5y-12x \\\\ x+3y\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, rewrite the order of the variables in the usual way:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}-12x+5y \\\\ x+3y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe require a $2\\times 2$ matrix $T$ such that\n    \n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-12x+5y \\\\ x+3y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-12 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-12x+5y \\\\ x+3y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n    Therefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-12 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}]}
